  "names": {
    "order": "given family",
    "conventions": "Given name then family name. Romanian surnames are the same for men and women and many end in -escu or -eanu (Popescu, Munteanu), while others are plain first names or trades (Radu, Ciobanu 'shepherd'). Plenty of people carry two given names, written with a hyphen or without (Ana-Maria, Ionuț Alexandru), and Orthodox name days such as Sfântul Ion or Sfânta Maria are celebrated like small birthdays. Diminutives are everyday: Ionuț, Andreiuț, Mihăiță, Irinuca. Hungarians, mostly in Transylvania, say the family name first in Hungarian (Nagy László) but Romanian papers write it given first; they keep Hungarian spellings with á, é, ő and ű.",
